{"title":"1986 AHSME Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A parabola <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24cf2d8efcb8217f3274aa19d98fa94af2df837d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = ax^{2} + bx + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"132\" height=\"18\" /> has vertex <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/b/7cb9265e7854534e5c082e16eb10470d08d46e1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4,2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c67f1e6c098104b1cb8f1cdd6bb16f689ac3e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" /> is on the parabola, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a81938ca5e71faa6894d9d52ac776c9efbe75d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$abc$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"27\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/f/fbf6231f948a62225e518cc825ec0560aad47906.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ -12\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ -6\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 0\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"411\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider the quadratic in completed square form: it must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba83a297d1400b096ff47aa04f3754ba6824c95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=a(x-4)^{2}+2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"137\" height=\"19\" />. Now substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/2/69271b422e022ea65ff1f288eddfcfa82afd8ab7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> to give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a9d8b938fb61f2d9e09ee86946c51333f1996bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"59\" height=\"37\" />. Now expanding gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee006a219417358609be693131ab6c8b3951f33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=-\\frac{1}{2}x^{2}+4x-6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"151\" height=\"37\" />, so the product is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3ccce19d0f6f6ecbe44f9c25c1492a7dfc431fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 4 \\cdot -6  = 3 \\cdot 4 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"183\" height=\"37\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/55206bce678ac0394d97dc04dd72398df2bdf572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{E}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AHSME_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text